00:41:23.430 --> 00:41:25.430
in terms of how we think about

00:41:25.430 --> 00:41:26.820
mental health in general?

00:41:26.820 --> 00:41:28.890
Both from what you've seen in your data

00:41:28.890 --> 00:41:30.840
and from a broader societal perspective.

00:41:30.840 --> 00:41:32.160
I realize that's a huge question

00:41:32.160 --> 00:41:35.350
but I'd love to hear your
thoughts on both of those.

00:41:35.350 --> 00:41:36.820
Bianca, if you wanna start.

00:41:36.820 --> 00:41:38.197
- Yes, I

00:41:38.197 --> 00:41:39.497
I want,

00:41:39.497 --> 00:41:40.330
I shouldn't say 'I want'

00:41:40.330 --> 00:41:41.930
'cause they're following the data.

00:41:41.930 --> 00:41:43.490
And what I believe is that

00:41:44.980 --> 00:41:47.730
biology has a setup for success

00:41:47.730 --> 00:41:49.287
not for failure.

00:41:49.287 --> 00:41:51.940
And any aspects that we're inheriting

00:41:51.940 --> 00:41:53.950
or any epigenetic component

00:41:53.950 --> 00:41:55.560
really in the proper framework

00:41:55.560 --> 00:41:58.470
is for us to succeed in that environment.

00:41:58.470 --> 00:41:59.440
Not to fail.

00:41:59.440 --> 00:42:01.223
Like evolution doesn't want
us to just crash and burn

00:42:01.223 --> 00:42:02.650
because it doesn't have a job.

00:42:02.650 --> 00:42:05.010
Like we talked about having a job.

00:42:05.010 --> 00:42:05.843
You can always tell, in 10 years

00:42:05.843 --> 00:42:07.468
when it's like, "the job"

00:42:07.468 --> 00:42:09.551
(laughs)

00:42:10.893 --> 00:42:12.610
If you need the job.

00:42:12.610 --> 00:42:14.991
Yeah, and so with that being said,

00:42:14.991 --> 00:42:16.320
I think that's the case.

00:42:16.320 --> 00:42:18.850
Like biology will always look out for us.

00:42:18.850 --> 00:42:20.020
That our brains and our bodies

00:42:20.020 --> 00:42:21.500
and those adaptations that it goes through

00:42:21.500 --> 00:42:22.930
will always look out for us.

00:42:22.930 --> 00:42:25.190
And so if we have the inkling to rest,

00:42:25.190 --> 00:42:26.890
we probably need to do that.

00:42:26.890 --> 00:42:28.620
We have the inkling,
whatever that rest looks like

00:42:28.620 --> 00:42:31.235
to you to pray, to take a second, to read,

00:42:31.235 --> 00:42:32.330
to hang out with your

00:42:32.330 --> 00:42:34.890
whatever that inkling is,
I suggest following that.

00:42:34.890 --> 00:42:35.990
And that's what I do in my life,

00:42:35.990 --> 00:42:38.000
because I trust my body's saying

00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:41.810
because humans haven't
been around for this long

00:42:41.810 --> 00:42:43.705
and we haven't knocked
ourselves off the planet yet.

00:42:43.705 --> 00:42:44.538
And so it's

00:42:44.538 --> 00:42:45.371
there's gotta be something there

00:42:45.371 --> 00:42:46.509
I should be listening to.

00:42:46.509 --> 00:42:47.342
